.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA POLICY - read before changing
#
# Everything under data/ is TRACKED on purpose. It is ~120 MB, the largest
# single file is 73 MB, and every byte of it is either a source the corpus is
# built from or the corpus itself. Losing it loses the project.
#
# The repository is PRIVATE (made private 2026-08-24), which is what makes
# that safe. Two licence questions in data/SOURCES.md are still open:
#   1. whether the BCS questions came from a redistributable source
#   2. what licence the released corpus carries (Wikipedia is CC BY-SA 4.0,
#      and share-alike likely propagates to anything derived from it)
#
# ==> BEFORE MAKING THIS REPOSITORY PUBLIC, close both questions, fix the
#     LICENSE file (it currently says MIT, which almost certainly cannot be
#     granted over CC BY-SA-derived content), and add the Wikipedia
#     attribution file that CC BY-SA requires. See SOURCES.md "Open actions".
#
# If question 1 comes back "not redistributable", uncomment the two lines
# below to untrack the source pool. The scripts rebuild it from scratch, so
# nothing is lost except the convenience of having it in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/raw/bn_qa_pool/*.jsonl
# data/interim/*.jsonl

# Annotation sheets.
#
# In-progress copies are ignored so two people can work in the same clone
# without colliding. FINISHED sheets are tracked on purpose: once a round is
# scored they are the evidence behind the kappa in the IAA report (DL3), and a
# result nobody can re-check is not a result.
data/annotated/**/items_*.csv
!data/annotated/**/items_for_annotation_BLANK.csv
!data/annotated/agreement_test_v1/items_for_annotation_tawhid.csv
!data/annotated/agreement_test_v1/items_for_annotation_shejan.csv

# The M3 round-1 sheets ARE tracked: they are the annotation itself, and losing
# them loses the labels. The private mapping is tracked too -- it is derived
# from data already in the repo, so hiding it protects nothing.
!data/annotated/round1/**

# Scratch
*.bak
/tmp/
scratch/
*.tmp

# Throwaway sanity splits from build_bn_pool.py. The real splits are
# data/splits/{train,dev,test}.jsonl, built by src/build_corpus.py.
data/splits/_pool_sanity/

# Formatted model inputs, rebuilt any time by src/preprocess.py. Keeping them out of
# git avoids a second, stale copy of the corpus drifting away from data/splits/.
data/processed/
